      "summary": "Skill 2.1.1 focuses on: 'Evaluate and select appropriate FMs from Amazon Bedrock based on task requirements and performance criteria.'. In modern enterprise machine learning and generative AI architectures, this topic forms the backbone of Task 2.1: Choose appropriate modeling approaches for ML and AI solutions under Domain 2: ML Model & Foundation Model (FM) Development. Rather than treating this as an isolated task, AWS assesses your end-to-end understanding of how data flows, how distributed compute is orchestrated, and how high availability, fault tolerance, and security compliance are enforced.\n\nAmazon Bedrock is the premier serverless AWS service for building generative AI applications using leading Foundation Models (FMs). It provides managed access to high-performance models from Anthropic (Claude 3.5 Sonnet, Claude 3 Haiku), Amazon (Titan Text, Titan Image, Titan Embeddings), Meta (Llama 3), Mistral AI, and AI21 Labs through a unified, secure API. Because Bedrock is completely serverless, you do not manage GPU infrastructure, clusters, or operating system patches.\n\nEnterprise customization on Bedrock spans three primary tiers: Prompt Engineering / Few-Shot prompting (zero compute cost, runtime context), Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) via Bedrock Knowledge Bases (connecting models to dynamic enterprise data in S3 and vector stores), and Fine-Tuning / Continuous Pre-training (customizing model weights using prompt-response pairs in JSONL format). For governance, Amazon Bedrock Guardrails applies configurable filters for PII redaction, toxic speech, denied topics, and hallucination grounding checks.",
