      "summary": "AWS Glue Data Quality is an official in-scope AWS service in the Analytics category for the AWS Machine Learning Engineer - Associate (MLA-C02) exam. In enterprise cloud environments, AWS Glue Data Quality provides robust, scalable, and highly available infrastructure specifically designed to address data engineering, deep learning model training, foundation model deployment, workflow orchestration, or cloud governance.\n\nWithin modern AWS ML/AI architectures, AWS Glue Data Quality plays an essential role. It integrates seamlessly with Amazon SageMaker AI, Amazon Bedrock, Amazon S3, and AWS IAM. Deploying AWS Glue Data Quality allows machine learning engineers to eliminate the operational toil of server provisioning, manual patching, and scaling bottlenecks while guaranteeing enterprise-grade SLAs, multi-AZ high availability, and rigorous compliance standards (such as HIPAA, GDPR, and SOC2).\n\nOn the MLA-C02 exam, questions surrounding AWS Glue Data Quality test your ability to make optimal architectural decisions under tight constraints. You must know precisely when AWS Glue Data Quality is the superior choice over competing AWS services, how to secure it using VPC Interface Endpoints (PrivateLink) and AWS KMS Customer Managed Keys (CMKs), how to configure least-privilege IAM policies, and how to optimize runtime costs.",
